# Lore any realm can talk about: Darkness Falls and Legion's court, the tunnels under the three frontiers,
# the dragons compared, con colours, drop superstitions, the world still finding itself, swimming to the
# edge of the world, old maps, hidden rooms, GM nights and player legends, and promised things that never
# came. Classic and Shrouded Isles (up to 1.65) only. New writing for this project.
#
# Truth rules for this file: documented lore is said plainly; rumours, superstitions and inventions are
# framed as hearsay, belief, memory or argument. No bot claims to have killed Legion, Behemoth, Govannon
# or a dragon. Realm * only: no place names except Darkness Falls and the battlegrounds, and every line
# that compares the realms treats all three the same.

@kind ambient
@topic lore
@realm *
@about place

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Darkness Falls: Legion's court
@who NoLifer
@levels 30-50
legion keeps a court down there like a king. princes, high lords, dukes, earls, marquises, and every demon knows its rank
[three demon princes|three princes] [sit|stand] under legion, and [each one|every one] of them would wipe a careless group
prince abdin, prince asmoien, prince ba'alorien. say them three times and see who shows up
the dukes in df are where most raids [find out|learn] [how big the gap is|they were not ready]
i like to think grand chancellor adremal keeps legion's books. even demons need clerks
field marshal nebir drills legion's army, or so the old raiders say
gatekeeper dommel has not left that door since df opened, or so the story goes
[heard|i hear] the chthonic knights stop [most raids|whole raids] long before anyone sees legion
legion takes less damage than you would think, or so every raid leader says after the wipe
[word is|heard] legion can send people straight into behemoth's room, and [that is the end of your evening|nobody walks back out]
even legion has a chamberlain. somebody has to sweep the floors
mutilator xagalith has the most honest title in the whole of darkness falls
i have walked past the dukes so often i know them by name. [alloc, aypol, bimure|sallis, satori, zepor], old neighbours
the earls down there have names no bard could rhyme. zh'alzhak, glassalab, ipostian, i ask you
back when df first opened nobody knew what a duke was. we learned on our corpses
i remember the first time someone typed legion in faction. the whole realm went quiet for a minute
nobody i know has seen every room in darkness falls, and i know some very stubborn people

@who NoLifer,Explorer
@levels 30-50
behemoth [cant be killed|does not die]. [every guild that tried says the same|i have heard it from three guilds], nothing sticks to him
people say behemoth takes no damage at all. others say nobody has brought enough people yet
level ninety nine and parked in a room doing nothing. behemoth is either guarding something or bored
[i think|my guess is] behemoth is not a monster at all, he is a lock, and nobody has found the key

@who *
@levels 20-50
the imps in df rob the bigger demons and trade the loot for seals. little thieves with a proper trade
a bright seal is worth more than a dull one, [even the imps know that|that is the whole df economy]
whoever holds the most keeps opens df. count the keeps before you pack
[df|darkness falls] changes hands [more often than the weather|like the weather]. check before you ride out
darkness falls was a story long before it was a dungeon. a few old timers swear they fought there in another life
[i like to think|i think] the demons were down there ages before any of us found the portal
[some say|people say] df feeds on the realm war. the more keeps change hands, the deeper it runs
they say the demons crawled up out of the deep once the three realms went to war with each other
ask an imp and i bet the realm war is the best thing that ever happened to them

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Summoner's Hall and Govannon
@who NoLifer,Explorer
@levels 35-50
grand summoner govannon starts the fight as an elf and finishes it as a demon. nobody knows which one is the real him
[the old raiders say|word is], leave govannon's shield node alone or [every hit does one damage|your swords might as well be sticks]
heard a govannon fight runs forty minutes. bring food, and a spare healer
aidon the archwizard waits in the summoner's hall like he owns it, and nobody can say whose side he is on
three summoners, an archwizard and sidhe guards, all in one hall. someone planned that
the summoners in that hall keep calling something. nobody i know has asked them what
[heard|people say] the deepest rooms of df lead to the summoner's hall, where all three realms come together
i heard the summoner's hall was a sidhe place before legion's lot moved in

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the tunnels and the third power
@who Explorer,NoLifer
@levels 20-50
someone dug tunnels under all three frontiers and filled them with undead. [who is the third power|nobody ever says who]
the tunnels under the frontier were not dug by albs, mids or hibs. something else wants all three of us
[i think|my guess is] the tunnels and the summoner's hall are one plan. someone is calling the dead from all three realms at once
the dead in the tunnels serve a power nobody has named, and i do not think it is legion
while three realms fight over keeps, something is digging under all of us. funny how that goes
every realm found tunnels under its own frontier, and every realm swears it found them first
i followed a tunnel [until my torch ran low|as far as i dared], and it went further than any map said
i bet whoever dug the tunnels also drew the old maps. explains a lot

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the dragons compared
@who *
@levels 30-50
wolf, stone or glimmer, which dragon is oldest? every realm says its own
three realms, three dragons. a wolf, a stone and a glimmer, and every realm thinks theirs is the worst
golestandt, gjalpinulva, cuuldurach. one for each realm, and every bard has a song for theirs
[heard|people say] the dragons have never met. probably for the best, one of them would eat the other two
[i think|my guess is] the three dragons are kin, scattered [across the realms|to the three realms] long before any of us
an old raid leader told me never nuke a dragon early. let the tanks get it settled first
half of every raid comes for the respec stones, not the loot. fifty stones a dragon
[those|the] luminescent stones are the real hoard. the dragon is only the lock on the chest
dragons drop nothing but coin, or so the bitter ones say
[heard|i hear] bring over a hundred people to a dragon and it [goes berserk|loses its temper]. so leave the cousins home
i heard dragons talk to your corpse after they kill you. not sure i want to know what they say
some swear killing the big giants nearby takes a dragon's fire away. i swear they are drunk
a dragon is just a big lizard until it breathes on you. then it is a religion
dragon lairs [smell of old coin and bad decisions|reek of burnt hair and regret]
i asked a town guard about the dragon once. he told me to go home. very helpful
heard the three dragons dream about each other. a bard probably made that up, but i like it
legend says the first group to find a dragon was a lost explorer who took a wrong turn
ask [an alb|a mid|a hib] and their dragon is the oldest. ask anyone else and you get two more answers
i remember when nobody knew the dragons existed, until some fool wandered into a lair

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the frontier giants
@who Explorer,Daredevil
@levels 25-50
each frontier has an old giant that belongs to no realm: a green knight, a glacier giant and evern. walk around them
[heard|people say] the glacier giant throws people [half a zone|clear across the frontier], and folks used to bet on where they land
the green knight leaves you alone unless you start it. wise people keep riding
[heard|i hear] evern gets healed by fairies landing on [its|the] stones. fairies first, always

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- con colours
@who *
@levels 10-50
the con colours lie. i once saw [an orange|a yellow] gut a full group
never trust a con on anything with a name. the colour is a mood, not a level
half the named mobs show one colour and hit like another, and the bestiaries cant agree either
purple is purple. there is no colour for run now, and there should be
my theory is the con colours were set by someone who never pulled anything
blue cons have killed more of us than reds ever did. nobody respects a blue

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- drop superstitions
@who Crafter
never say the item's name in chat while you camp it. my old guild swore the mob hears
[my old guild|an old guildmate] swore drops are better if you /bow to the corpse before looting
some people think rare drops come right after a server reset. i think they just remember the good nights
i knew a crafter who would not loot with a full bag. said the rare could tell
first kill after you log in [always|never] drops the good stuff, depending who you ask
[old wisdom says|they say] drops improve the moment the whole camp stops talking about them
i keep a lucky ring in my pack for rare drops. it has not worked once. still wont sell it
dragon scales would make amazing armor, if only someone would let crafters near one
@who *
the stealth folk claim drops come better if you open from behind. of course they would
a healer friend never loots first. says the luck follows whoever was humble
if the named pops right as you go afk, [that is not luck, that is a curse|that is a curse], and everyone knows it
never camp one spot too long after dark. old superstition says the camp starts noticing

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the world finding itself
@who Explorer
the islands just turned up one autumn, [as if they had always been there|like they were always there]. bet there are more
every realm has a story about a pass that came out of the mist one day where no pass had been
there is always one more dungeon nobody has found yet. always
every year someone finds a new cave and [everyone acts surprised|acts surprised]. i stopped being surprised
[i bet|i think] the world goes further than any map they sell
[the old maps|my old map] [show|shows] roads that are not there anymore. either the mapmaker was drunk or the world moved
i still keep a first map with half the coast missing. it was more honest
the old maps had whole stretches marked unknown. best part of the map
half the fun early on was not knowing what was over the next hill
nobody charted the far corners properly. i swear there are caves nobody mentions
i keep a journal of spots i stumbled into that show up on no map
every realm has a tale about a lost place that the older maps almost show
some sages say the gods are still drawing the world, one island at a time
the bards claim the land was half the size at the start, and it grows a little each year
heard there is a vendor out in the wilds who sells maps of places that do not exist yet
when i see a ledge nobody talks about, in i go. usually it is just a bear
found a ruined wall once that nobody could name. still wondering whose it was
every ridge looks climbable right up until you slide back down
i could swear the fog out past the coast moves when nobody is looking
a sage told me the fog at the edge of the world is the gods' unfinished work. makes sense to me
real explorers never ask directions. we get lost on purpose
best kind of evening: no group, no plans, just riding toward a coastline nobody bothered with
i still wonder who carved the old markers out in the wilds. half of them point at nothing
[an old|a] [hunter|ranger|scout] swore the wild beasts remember the old roads the maps forgot
heard of a guy who logged out on a rock at the edge of the world and logged in somewhere nobody recognised

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the edge of the world
@who Explorer
every map ends in water, but the water does not end. swim far enough and you hit the wall the gods put there
i once swam out until the water went dark. then nothing, just a wall you cannot see
[heard|people say] if you swim far enough out the [fog gets thicker|water turns grey], and then there is just a wall
a friend swam to the edge of the world and came back saying the sky just stops
[i think|my theory is] the wall at the edge is there to keep something out, not to keep us in
the edge of the world is real, i swam into it. like cold glass under the sea
nobody can say what is beyond the wall. i asked a sage once, he told me to go level
a swim to the edge takes forever. bring patience, the view is worth it
heard there is an island out past the last map's edge that you can see but never reach
@who Daredevil
[i dare|dare] anyone to swim to the edge [in full plate|in their armor] and back
one day i will swim to the edge with no speed buff, just to say i did

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- hidden rooms
@who Explorer
every dungeon has a room behind the room. never found one myself, but i check every wall
[heard|people say] there is a wall in one of the old dungeons that only opens [when nobody is watching|for a group of one class]
i once walked along every wall of a dungeon hunting a secret door. all i found was [a rat|a spider]
some corners in the old dungeons look built for something that never moved in. gives me chills
an old bard told me every crypt has one sealed room nobody opens. i half believe it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- GM nights and player legends
@who Socialite
i remember a gm night where the whole town turned out for a poetry contest. weirdest evening in years
heard a gm once held a funeral for a player right out in the frontier. i like to think nobody attacked
every realm has a legend about one player who held a bridge alone. i believe all of them
heard of a [bard|minstrel|skald] who dragged a whole camp across a zone and lived. [probably a lie|i want it to be true]
you hear about healers who never died once all the way to fifty. nobody i know has met one
old raid leaders turn into legends faster than the dragons do
some names in the old herald rankings feel more like myth than people now
i swear i once saw a gm stroll through a town in a funny hat. nobody believes me
[rumour is|they say] a gm sometimes rides the roads [in disguise|disguised as a nobody]. be polite to strangers, just in case
word is the imps know every rumour in all three realms. i should ask them
the best part of a good legend is that nobody can prove anything
[heard|people say] the old gods still walk the roads now and then. i wave at every stranger
nothing beats a good ghost story at the bind stone

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- promised things
@who NoLifer
the devs promised more relics years ago. still six on the pedestals
six relics, two per realm. there were supposed to be more. i keep wondering where they are
[i think|my theory is] the missing relics are buried out there, waiting for someone to stumble on them
some say the other relics were never made. i like the version where they sit in a chest somewhere
every patch someone swears new relics are coming. every patch, nothing
we were promised more relics back at the start. we got islands instead
every realm guards two relics and swears its pair is the oldest
albs have their lost city, mids have their lost hall, hibs have their door under the hill. everyone has a place they cant find

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- general lore musings
@who *
every realm swears its legends are the oldest. i think all three are right
legends never die, they just grow another verse each time a bard sings them
half of lore is people who wiped explaining why
the oldest lesson in the game: if it has a name, it has a grudge
the battlegrounds have their own ghosts too. every one has a hill where someone stood against ten
heard a renegade chieftain in the battlegrounds remembers every face that ever beat him
nobody ever explains why the dead keep getting up in all three realms. we just kill them twice

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- is it worth it, and dares
@who Leveler
@levels 30-50
dragon raids are three hours of standing around for a stone. i will level instead
df is decent xp while your realm holds it, and useless the rest of the week
legion lore is fun, but lore never gave anyone a bubble
@who Daredevil
@levels 30-50
i dare someone to run up to behemoth just to wave. once
one day i will tag a duke in df alone, just to see what happens
someday i will stand where legion can see me and not run. someday

# ================================================================ debates
@kind debate
@realm *

@topic lore_behemoth
@levels 30-50
@scene lore_behemoth_killable
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Daredevil
@role D type=*
A: behemoth cant be killed, right | {q} is it true nobody can kill behemoth | is behemoth really unkillable or is that just a story
B: every guild that ever tried says he soaks it all up | never heard of a raid that left a mark on him | the old raiders say he shrugs off every hit
C: nobody brought enough people, thats all | everything dies if you hit it long enough | they said the dragons couldnt die once too
B: level ninety nine and no damage taken. that is not a numbers problem | you could bring the whole realm and he would yawn
C: then why put him there at all. a mob nobody can kill is a lock waiting for a key | something that cant die is a door, not a monster
?D: maybe he guards legion, not the other way round | i heard legion sends people to his room as a punishment
A: so either a lock or a wall | either way i am not volunteering | well i am not walking in to test it
C: i would. one day | someday i will | dare me

@topic lore_tunnels
@levels 20-50
@scene lore_third_power
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=NoLifer
@role D type=Socialite
A: who actually dug the tunnels under the frontiers | {q} whose work are those tunnels under all three frontiers | the tunnels under the frontier, who dug them
B: undead did the digging, but undead dont plan | the dead dug them, someone else told them where | skeletons with shovels, but somebody drew the plans
C: legion. who else wants all three realms at once | it is the demons, it has to be | my money is on legion, he hates all three of us the same
B: the tunnels feel older than df though | the stonework down there is not demon work | demons dont dig, they crawl up
D: my guild says it is a power nobody has met yet | i heard a bard say the old gods are testing us | maybe the dead are just bored
C: no realm would waste that much stone on the dead | whatever it is, it is not one of us three
B: i followed one until it split three ways, one way per realm | i think they all meet under the summoner's hall
?D: at least it treats all three realms fairly | so whoever it is wants all of us the same
A: a third power, then. lovely | so nobody knows. figures | great, something else to lose sleep over

@topic lore_dragons
@levels 30-50
@scene lore_oldest_dragon
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=*
A: wolf, stone or glimmer, settle it, which dragon came first | {q} which of the three dragons is the oldest | which dragon is oldest, the wolf, the stone or the glimmer
B: stone. granite does not get young | the stone one, nothing is older than rock | stone, the hills were there before anything
C: the glimmer. anything that old turns to light in the end | glimmer, it lives half in another world and those dont age
D: the wolf. wolves were here before anyone built a hut | the wolf one, the oldest stories all start with a wolf
B: a wolf is just a dog with ambition | wolves die of old age, stone does not
D: stones crack and glimmers fade, the wolf keeps hunting | rock just sits there, a wolf survives
?C: maybe they hatched together and split up | three eggs, one nest, three realms
A: so three answers, same as always | i asked one question and got three dragons | ok, every realm has the oldest one

@topic lore_dragons
@levels 30-50
@scene lore_dragon_sex
@role B type=Socialite
@role C type=NoLifer
@role D type=*
A: are the dragons he or she | {q} he or she, when we talk about the dragons | settle a bet, are the dragons male or female
B: the heralds call the stone one she | i always heard the stone one is a she
C: the glimmer king is the only male, it is in the name | glimmer KING, that one at least is easy
B: and the wolf? people say he and she in the same raid | the wolf gets called both, sometimes in one sentence
C: whoever gets breathed on gets to decide | when it is breathing on you, you do not check
?D: maybe dragons do not bother with any of that | it is a dragon, it is whatever it wants to be
A: so one she, one he, one depends who you ask | ok, she, he, and argue about the third

@topic lore_cons
@levels 10-50
@scene lore_con_colours
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Daredevil
@role D type=*
A: do the con colours lie or is it just me | {q} anyone else think the con colours lie | i swear the colours lie sometimes
B: they lie on named mobs. on normal ones they are fair | named mobs always hit above their colour | the colour is right, the named ones just cheat
C: colours are a suggestion. red is a challenge | i pull purples to see what happens, the colour means nothing
B: and that is why you see your bind point more than your camp | which is why you are always running back
C: you see more of the world on the run back | the run back is half the fun
?D: yellows are the sneaky ones, they look fair and then they crit | the worst are the ones that con blue and fight like orange
A: so trust the colour, unless it has a name | ok. green means go, everything else means maybe

@topic lore_drops
@levels 35-50
@scene lore_dragon_loot
@role B type=Crafter
@role C type=Leveler
@role D type=*
A: do dragons really drop nothing but coin | {q} is it true the dragons only drop coin | heard dragon loot is a joke, true
B: the stones are the real prize. fifty respec stones a kill | the respec stones are what everyone comes for
C: hours of waiting for a respec i will use once | i could level twice in the time a raid takes to form
B: you will want it when your spec is a mess at fifty | ask anyone who regretted their spec at forty
A: and the armor? | no armor at all?
B: i heard about one cloak once. one | the good pieces turn up, just never for the person telling the story
?D: i go for the screenshot. a dragon corpse is worth a hundred items | i just want to see one fall, loot or no loot
C: so the loot is a rumour and the stones are real | fine, stones are real, everything else is a story
A: still going next time | ok, still signing up | i am still going, for the story

